author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "At least one structural graph property beyond a degree count is computed by an automated surface and compared against a declaration, so a record whose lineage collapses to a spine fails rather than passes; The audit profile exposes the structural properties the graph analytics already compute, so a consumer does not have to re-run and re-parse a second subcommand to reach them; Every graph subcommand either has a named automated consumer or is recorded as deliberately interactive-only, and the classification is data rather than an absence of references; The typed reachability of terminal items to an outcome is measured over the whole record rather than the active scope, so a property that only holds for the current frontier cannot report as satisfied; A negative control proves the new structural check fails on a record whose typed relationships have been stripped to a spine"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "The SDK graph audit now projects structural cut metrics, exhaustive findings, and typed all-status outcome reachability into native assurance."
expected_result: "A structural collapse or loss of typed outcome reachability fails an automated declaration, and every graph operation has an explicit consumer disposition."
actual_result: "Articulation, bridge, active/terminal reachability, and finding census assertions pass with negative controls; all 16 operations are inventoried."
